    {
      "id": "claim_8b3108a23f50480bbc9c056e71ef4745",
      "statement": "Every tsc run is forced single-threaded because tsgo's default parallel checkers each keep separate type caches and re-derive capnweb's recursive type graphs, making single-threaded both faster and smaller; standalone app tsconfigs mirror the setting.",
